# Build products and caches that must not travel into the build context.
#
# `src/edutap/pass_builder/ui/static/` is the one that matters: it is where a
# local `make build-frontend` writes, and `COPY src ./src` would carry that
# bundle into the image ALONGSIDE the one the frontend stage builds. The two
# differ -- the local one is built for base "/" and the image's for the
# deployment's mount point -- and the result is an image shipping a second,
# wrong bundle that nothing references and nobody notices.
src/edutap/pass_builder/ui/static/
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/openapi.json

.venv/
.git/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
docs/_build/
.env
